// no-split-suggestion-dispatch — one-transaction suggestion insertion (precedent #58).
//
// A `@tiptap/suggestion` surface that deletes its trigger range and then
// inserts content MUST land both in ONE dispatched transaction. Dispatching
// the trigger-delete on its own opens a window: `view.dispatch` runs
// `updateState` synchronously, and anything it fires re-entrantly during the
// delete's own dispatch (a plugin `appendTransaction`, a plugin-view or
// NodeView update, an `editor.on('transaction')` listener, or the
// y-prosemirror binding reacting to the just-applied delete) can dispatch a
// transaction that remaps the selection onto an adjacent `selectable: true`
// node — the follow-up insert then REPLACES that node. Silent data loss, no
// error, load-dependent (reads as e2e flake).
//
// The rule fires INSIDE a `Suggestion({ ... })` config on the two
// bare-trigger-delete dispatch shapes:
//
//   1. `....deleteRange(range).run()` — a chain whose FINAL step before
//      `.run()` is the delete. A compliant atomic chain always continues past
//      the delete (`.deleteRange(range).insertContent(...).run()`, or the
//      slash boundary's `.deleteRange(range).command(...).run()`), so the
//      receiver of its `.run()` is never the `deleteRange` call itself.
//   2. `editor.commands.deleteRange(range)` — the `commands.*` form always
//      dispatches immediately, so inside a suggestion `command` it is a
//      standalone trigger-delete transaction by construction.
//
// Fix: compose delete + insert into one chain, or route through a boundary
// like `applySlashCommandItem` (`packages/app/src/editor/slash-command/
// apply-item.ts`) when items need post-commit work (`afterCommit`).
//
// Does NOT catch (documented honestly):
//   - A split where the delete chain carries an unrelated non-content step
//     before `.run()` (e.g. `.deleteRange(r).focus().run()`) — the receiver
//     of `.run()` is then not the `deleteRange` call. Focus-first ordering
//     (`.focus().deleteRange(r).run()`) IS caught (shape 1).
//   - A second dispatch made by the ITEM the command delegates to (an
//     `item.command(editor)` that runs its own `editor.chain().run()`).
//     Lint can't see through the delegation; the runtime pins in
//     `suggestion-atomicity.dom.test.tsx` + `slash-command-atomicity.dom.test.tsx`
//     assert the exactly-one-doc-changing-transaction invariant end to end.
//   - A raw `view.dispatch(tr.delete(...))` inside a Suggestion config —
//     no occurrence today; add a shape if one appears.
//
// Suppress a legitimate exception (a Suggestion surface that deletes its
// trigger WITHOUT ever inserting — none exists today) with:
//   // biome-ignore lint/plugin/no-split-suggestion-dispatch: <reason>

language js

or {
    `Suggestion($config)` where {
        $config <: contains `$chain.deleteRange($range).run()` as $bare,
        register_diagnostic(
            span = $bare,
            message = "Split suggestion dispatch: this chain dispatches the trigger-range delete on its own. Compose the delete and the insert into ONE chain (`.deleteRange(range).insertContent(...).run()`) or route through an applySlashCommandItem-style boundary so the item contributes steps to the same transaction (precedent #58). A separately dispatched delete lets a re-entrant transaction remap the selection and the follow-up insert silently replace an adjacent node. See https://github.com/inkeep/open-knowledge/blob/main/biome-plugins/README.md#no-split-suggestion-dispatchgrit"
        )
    },
    `Suggestion($config)` where {
        $config <: contains `$editor.commands.deleteRange($range)` as $cmd,
        register_diagnostic(
            span = $cmd,
            message = "Split suggestion dispatch: `commands.deleteRange` dispatches the trigger-range delete immediately as its own transaction. Compose the delete and the insert into ONE chain (`.deleteRange(range).insertContent(...).run()`) or route through an applySlashCommandItem-style boundary so the item contributes steps to the same transaction (precedent #58). See https://github.com/inkeep/open-knowledge/blob/main/biome-plugins/README.md#no-split-suggestion-dispatchgrit"
        )
    }
}
